WEBVTT

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.250
Hey, Mr. Clown.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.960
I’ve finished baking as well.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.000
Oh my!

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.960
Your bread is wonderful!

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.920
Of course, the rose piercing the bread is beautiful...

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.170
but the bread itself looks delicious.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.680
This is truly worthy of the first theme
of our clothing, food and shelter topic.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.720
It’s a really artistic bread.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.020
And in stark comparison... What is that?

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.120
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.080
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.450
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.920
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:59.040
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:02.760
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.060
Pierrot escorted away!?

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.350
The bread packed tightly with love!

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.340
Suwabara...

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.680
Far from being artistic, your bread is merely burnt black.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.010
There’s no competition at all with this.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:51.060
To think that a world-level clown
such as yourself couldn’t figure this out...

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.860
Don’t misunderstand.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.230
All I said was that I was done with the baking.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.580
This is...!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.080
It’s a crown!

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.670
I see!

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.090
That’s what it was!

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:18.710
What do you mean?

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.090
Suwabara made two different doughs.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.220
One of those was croissant dough.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:29.260
The other was the dough for the pane di oro,
which forms the base of that crown.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:32.940
Pane di oro originated in
Italy and means “golden bread.”

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.850
The dough is yellow and goopy before baking,

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:39.480
since it uses more egg yolk than castella or brioche.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:42.110
After baking, it becomes a golden color.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:46.660
But, if you want to bake a soft
bread when the original dough is goopy,

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.120
you have to bake it in a mold.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.450
And the surface that’s in
contact with the mold will turn brown.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.120
In order to protect against that,

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.210
he coated the inner surface of the
mold with a thin layer of croissant dough.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:05.050
That’s kinda... similar to my
<i>Japan</i> #43, the 324-layer croissant.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.260
Yeah, the underlying principle is the same.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.180
Moreover, in the case of this bread, since it’s delicate,

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.230
this allows him to take it out of
the mold without destroying its shape.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:19.230
But, when did he make the mold?

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:23.190
You remember that he’d been fighting with a
log in the middle of the road some time back?

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:27.080
Oh, now that you mention it,
it was shaped like a crown.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.530
That’s right.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.080
That was the prototype for the mold.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.200
After that, I had myself introduced
to a blacksmith at the Royal Palace.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.080
And I made the mold myself.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.580
By... By yourself?!

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.790
I’ve made a sword by myself.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.590
Looks like I may have jumped to conclusions.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.140
As long as you understand that.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.090
But...

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.010
that’s not all there is to it!

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.190
That’s chocolate!

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.980
He’s outlining the fruit with chocolate!

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.360
That’s all it is and yet...

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.820
it looks like the fruit is floating!

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.950
But why do something like that...?

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:11.200
This time, his bread is completely yellow.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.770
He must have thought that
without creating those shadows,

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:16.960
the shine of the fruit would be overpowered by the gold of the bread.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.710
Both contestants have shown
a wonderful set of strategies.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:25.220
I can’t really judge their
quality now without tasting them.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:28.800
So, since Monica’s bread was
completed first, I’ll start with her...

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.180
Uh, time out.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:34.430
If Samurai Boy would prefer it,
I don’t mind you sampling my bread later.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:35.690
What?

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:37.930
Why say something like that?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.310
No matter what the bread, it’s
most delicious when freshly baked.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:42.690
And she...

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:43.980
I smell something fishy!

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:46.440
Sample Naked Woman’s bread first, Pierrot!

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.150
Oh, don’t be like that.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.700
You don’t need to hold back.
There’s no need to be distant.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.530
Distant?!

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:57.160
I mean... in a way, we’ve
spent “naked time” together, right?

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.540
Don’t say things like that!

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.670
So what will you do, Suwabara?

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:07.670
Very well.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.090
Sample mine first.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:10.180
Okay then!

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.430
Then, getting right to it...

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.430
Something’s strange.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:15.850
There’s no doubt that Naked Woman’s bread

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:20.350
has something to it that requires time.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.810
But...

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:26.820
A true warrior must defeat his
opponent when they are at their strongest.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.580
So, I will accept your challenge head on.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:35.580
So, regret the fact that you permitted my pane di oro Kai to be eaten while it was still fresh.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.120
Pi~errot.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:50.720
A box?

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.470
That’s silly. It’s really obvious.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:54.430
What is?

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:57.350
If you’re a person used to reactions, then...

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:01.690
Pane di oro... Pandora... Pandora’s Box.
It’s obvious where he’s going.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:05.690
Also, it’s written in three languages that the box should absolutely not be opened.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.730
What’s Pandora’s Box?

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:09.200
Don’t you know?

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.610
Long ago, God had locked all
the world’s miseries into a box.

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.700
And he’d ordered that the box
should not be opened at any cost.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.740
What are miseries?

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:21.290
Geez, you don’t even know that?

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:24.830
It refers to the calamities and
misfortunes that befall a person.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:30.220
And, since a girl called Pandora broke the order and opened the box,

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:33.760
all the miseries were let out into the human world.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.470
It’s a Greek myth.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:43.520
So, if we open that, will those “miseries” things fly out at us?

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:47.020
Now that you mention it... That’s true...

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:48.810
Hey, Naked Woman.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.020
Help me open this.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:51.270
It’s pretty heavy.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.980
My name is not Naked Woman.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.530
It’s Monica. Monica.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:56.610
Who cares about your name?!

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:59.530
Either way, unless we open this,
the judging won’t go anywhere.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:01.040
All right.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.040
D-Don’t do that, Suwabara!

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.040
Heave-ho.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.510
Th... This is...?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.510
Chinese cabbage?

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:25.980
Chinese cabbages flew out from Pandora’s Box?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:30.610
Hakusai. Hakusai. Hakusai. Hakusai. Hakusai.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.400
Yakusai.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:32.610
Yakusai!

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.450
So, Chinese cabbages came out
from Pandora’s Box instead of miseries?!

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.260
Wanna eat?

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:40.120
What are these?!
Would you like to eat?

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:40.610
Miseries are upon us!
What are these?!
Would you like to eat?

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.250
Miseries are upon us!

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.290
Buy some stock?

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.300
Let’s make some money.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.040
Suwabara!

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:54.750
I believe that according to the legend,
after all the miseries had been released,

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.970
Pandora found hope in the box in the end.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.770
And thus, I believe that hope was left behind in the human world.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:05.100
I’m sure that Pierrot is thinking-along the same lines.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.770
Find that hope quickly!

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:08.770
Roger!

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.480
What’s wrong?

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.480
Hurry up.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.480
This is...

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:17.650
I’m not sure if this is hope...

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:21.530
I think this is a burdock root.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.000
Why is a burdock root...?

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.880
Gobou. Gobou. Gobou. Gobou. Gobou. Gobou.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.000
Kibou?!

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:38.510
Kibou!

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.630
Geez, do something about this already.

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:46.220
Pierrot?!

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:47.720
It was you after all!

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:02.200
All the Chinese cabbages went back into the box.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.120
Once you’re a world-level clown,

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:11.590
you have to learn to use various
wild beasts just as you use your limbs.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:15.590
So, controlling a few
Chinese cabbages is a piece of cake.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.840
Chinese cabbages are wild beasts, huh?

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:22.600
More importantly, how do all those Chinese cabbages fit into a box like that?

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:26.830
Nevertheless, Suwabara’s bread was amazing.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.730
His strategy of using croissant dough on the surface,

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:32.440
thus ensuring that the inner dough
would remain unburnt and golden...

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.110
Also, his strategy to create those shadows...

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.280
And his strategy regarding the fruit.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:40.120
It was truly spectacular.

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:42.620
I believe that many of you must have noticed, but...

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:48.120
The fruits that Suwabara used
were shining like jewels, right?

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:49.630
Now that he mentions it...

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:53.630
He used a special honey for that!

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:55.380
Right, Suwabara?

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.510
Impressive as always, Pierrot.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:59.510
But, you’ve made one mistake.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.850
The honey I used was not special.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:05.860
It was just regular honey!

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:07.060
Huh?

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:12.070
After Being defeated by Azuma in the Pantasia newcomers’ battle, I began to create <i>Lupan</i>.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:14.730
In order to steal breadmaking techniques from around the world,

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:17.360
I studied with all I had every day.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.780
No! No! No!

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.950
Far from defeating Azuma,

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:28.870
I can’t even defeat strong people
around the world with just these techniques.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:29.790
Kai!

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:34.550
This time, upon losing in your battle with
the bread, you’re taking it out on the books?!

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.840
You even sliced the library card!

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:40.550
Hiromi-chan, the librarian, will get mad at me again.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:41.890
Master.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:42.970
Listen up, Kai.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:46.560
I did tell you to steal bread techniques.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:50.350
But, it’s not just techniques
relating to bread that you must steal.

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:54.570
The true swordsman concerns himself with

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:58.070
the beauty of the sheath and the hilt,
in addition to that of the sword.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.530
I believe that bread is the same.

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.700
In addition to bread, you must study more about

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:07.950
the processing of foods like fruit, hams and cheeses that go with it.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:11.000
Only then will you be a true bread artisan, right?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.080
The processing of foods?

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:17.050
Once he helped me realize that,
I once again applied myself to study.

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:18.590
And I came across a certain book.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:20.430
A German book.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:21.550
German?

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.720
That’s my country!

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:27.100
That book had this written in it.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.060
Germany has a custom of storing dry fruit in honey for

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:33.350
long periods of time at the end
of the year, and then eating them.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:37.320
On doing that, the flavor
becomes richer and very delicious.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.110
W-Wait a moment.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:41.820
It’s true that Germany has such a custom.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.240
But the fruit doesn’t shine all that much.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.830
That’s true.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:50.710
But, I mixed already smashed fruit with honey,

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:54.830
added color to the honey
itself, and added even more fruit.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:58.000
With this, the color of the fruit was deepened.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:03.840
And thanks to the luster of the
colored honey, the fruit shone like jewels.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.550
After that, I just applied croissant
dough to the surface of the mold,

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:08.680
and attached the fruit on the inside.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:12.350
In this way, I could arrange them in any manner I wanted.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.220
I’ve eaten dry fruit preserved in honey

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:20.650
many a time with Mama and Papa at the year-end celebrations.

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.660
But, I never came up with such a strategy.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.580
You’re pretty good, Samurai Boy.

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:33.080
But... it’s not like I don’t have a
great trick of my own up my sleeve.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:37.460
But, that’s an amazing
technique Suwabara’s stolen there.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:38.590
It’s amazing.

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:41.630
Our victory is a sure thing now.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.590
No, we still don’t know who’ll win the match.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:46.590
And what’s truly amazing is...

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:50.100
the fact that you haven’t
noticed how far your wig has slipped.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.520
All right.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:54.100
I’ll start with sampling Monica’s bread now.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:55.600
Oh?

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:57.440
This is...?

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.610
The flower has blossomed!!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:00.610
What?!

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:01.610
What was that?!

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.110
H-How can that be?!

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.530
Monica, she...

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:09.120
By mixing a little starch syrup with the
solution she used to glue the petals together,

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:13.450
she worked it so that the petals would bloom because of the heat and gravity.

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.120
Is that even possible?!

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.250
Yeah.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:19.170
The temperature of this room,
the heat given off by the dough,

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.420
the heat produced due to the illumination provided by the overhead lights...

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:28.510
When putting all three together, it’s
possible to soften the starch syrup portion.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:31.720
But...

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.680
the risk of this technique failing is quite high.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:36.480
Unless you have absolute confidence in yourself,

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:40.110
you can’t use such a laborious
technique in the all-important finals.

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:42.900
She’s fearsome. Monica Adenauer.

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:43.610
Bang.
Just as expected of the patisserie world champion!

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.650
Just as expected of the patisserie world champion!

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.660
That was sly!

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:52.160
Because you had this trick set up,
you wanted me to go first, right?

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.160
Yep!

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:55.500
This woman...

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.670
It seems that she’s really not
just an ordinary naked woman.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:00.210
Interesting.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.670
Let’s see all that you have.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:05.970
Oh, that was an amazing trick, Monica.

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:10.180
Also, even though quite some
time has passed, this bread is still hot.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:13.640
You have more tricks up your sleeve, don’t you?

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.680
Of course!

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.190
In fact, this is where the fun really starts.

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:19.230
Oh, I’m looking forward to that.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:20.690
Then, right away, let’s...

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:25.190
I can’t call myself a top baker in the world yet.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:25.990
But...

00:15:25.990 --> 00:15:30.450
I believe that this bread should
at least do well at the world level.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:34.240
After all, it’s packed with my mother’s love.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.040
I... I don’t believe it!

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:45.050
It’s world-level unbelievable.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:50.050
This is the first time I’ve ever
eaten such a wonderful bread!

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:51.800
What?!

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:56.390
Operator, please connect this mic to the outside.

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:58.480
What number would you like to dial?

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:00.020
Number 17.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:05.530
Huh? He seems to be telephoning someplace...

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:08.570
Number 17 is equivalent to the Japanese 110.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.280
In other words, it’s the police.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:11.530
Police?!

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:12.070
Monaco Police

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.780
This is the Monaco Police Department.
Monaco Police

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.030
Is something the matter?
Monaco Police

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:15.040
Is something the matter?

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:18.790
You see, actually I’ve been agitating Chinese cabbages.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.040
N-No way!

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:30.550
But, we’re right in the middle of
the finals of a world tournament.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:33.050
Old Man Pierrot has been arrested...

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:35.050
and has been escorted away.

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.100
He was escorted away.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.640
Escorted away?!

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:40.520
I see!

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.890
Hey, what in the world is happening?!

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:46.360
What’s happened to the judging of my bread?!

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:47.570
Don’t panic.

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:50.400
He’s a world-level examiner.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.780
I’m sure that his being
convoyed away is part of some plan.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:56.490
I’m sure that if we wait for a while,
the judging will be carried out.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.280
I wonder...

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:02.120
Pierrot has just been arrested for the
crime of agitating the Chinese cabbages,

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:06.790
which goes against Monaco’s laws concerning prevention of public annoyance.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:08.670
While it may be his first crime,

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.460
he won’t be coming back home today at the very least.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:11.800
Huh?!

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.300
Then, what are we supposed to do?!

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:16.300
You have no choice but to go and visit him.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:17.800
Visit him?

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:22.810
I’m sorry about having you come all the way here.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:25.480
More importantly, please get on with the judging.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:26.310
Yeah!

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:31.190
You haven’t assessed my bread at all after eating it!

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.320
Okiedokie.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.070
Say, Kuro-yan...

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.160
Why don’t we go in as well?

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.280
Yeah.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:41.910
I want to see the inside of a
police station at least once.

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:42.540
No!

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.080
Why not?

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.790
You want to see your friend lose?

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:52.050
I lose?!

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:54.630
From times immemorial,

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:58.260
the combination of sour rye bread with sweet candy has been considered good.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:01.890
Up until there, it’s pretty ordinary.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:06.730
But, Monica’s bread had a trick to it
that nobody could have imagined.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.060
What do you mean?!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:12.020
Here, look closely at the spot that I’ve bitten into.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:13.780
The... The dough has...

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:15.320
Five layers you say?!

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.320
Yeah.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.050
During the match,

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:22.330
Monica had made five doughs with varying amounts of rye and wheat flour, right?

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.540
She probably glued those together with candy,

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:29.330
and piled them on top of each other like
a sandwich to make a five-layered bread.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.300
D-Don’t tell me that’s why Pierrot...

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:34.170
Yeah, there’s no doubt about it.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.340
That’s why Pierrot...

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.800
allowed himself to be convoyed!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.100
What an examiner!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.810
To think that he’d get himself arrested for a reaction?!

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:47.390
I guess you would not understand this, but...

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.770
that’s the kind of person a judge is.

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:51.560
What kind of person is that?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.360
Leaving that aside,

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:57.650
what’s so special about having
five layers glued together by candy?

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:59.160
Yeah?

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:00.870
Well, firstly...

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:01.570
It’s heat retention.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:04.580
Candy gets hot more easily than bread.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:08.500
If candy is integrated inside, the heat
retention capacity of the bread is heightened.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.220
And the bread won’t cool down,

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:13.590
even during the time it takes for the candy rose sculpture to bloom.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.800
Also, in terms of the display...

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.550
The bread looks like the strata of the Earth.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:21.890
And the candy within looks like ground water.

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:26.600
It looks like the rose really is
absorbing water, which is just cute.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:28.560
Wh... What does it taste like?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.600
That’s just superb.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:34.980
Hamburger buns are split at a ratio of 4:6, right?

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:37.740
I’ll explain it in more detail in
the seed of knowledge section.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:41.110
You’re going to leave it for the
seed of knowledge section again?

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:46.200
Monica also adjusted the appropriate ratios into the layers of the bread.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:50.120
The five-layered bread has
been constructed as shown here.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:53.830
By controlling the ratio of the rye flour,
which is heavier than wheat flour,

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:56.760
she has set up a miraculous balance here.

00:19:56.760 --> 00:20:00.760
Also, she’s made the second layer
quite light, while the first layer is heavy.

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.680
This is probably the result
of testing various possibilities.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:05.400
She probably figured that it would taste better

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:09.520
if the first layer was heavy,
as it would form the outer crust.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.940
As expected of a world-level examiner.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:16.150
That’s exactly right.

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:19.650
And no matter what, you
just don’t get tired of this bread.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:23.110
After all, there are five different tastes to this bread.

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:25.570
You just don’t get tired of it.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:27.620
I’m sorry, Suwabara.

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:30.410
Your bread was also wonderful, but...

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.960
This bread had a trick to it such that you never get sick of it.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.900
It surpasses the strategy applied to your bread,

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.840
as it made me feel something like a deep love.

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:40.840
I’ve lost completely.

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:42.680
Oh stop that.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:44.390
There’s no need to be depressed.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:46.100
You’re a samurai, right?

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:51.100
Actually, it was my mother who
came up with the idea of the five layers.

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.650
I was tired of eating the same thing every day,

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:57.610
and this was what she came up with
to make me eat nutritious food.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:00.110
This is the fruit of my mother’s love.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:03.650
So, my win this time is thanks to my mother.

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:06.320
I had no hope of winning with just my skill.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.620
After fighting with you, I understood this.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:12.410
As a baker, your skill is impressive.

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:13.830
So, you should be confident in that.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.790
Doesn’t get any worse than this.

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:18.840
To think that I’m being comforted by a girl.

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:21.340
But, it’s the truth!

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:25.890
What? You don’t know what a handshake is?

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:28.850
I thought that a handshake was a universal custom.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:30.850
But...

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:35.850
I just wish to engrave upon this hand
that I fought with a marvelous artisan.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.150
That’s not really necessary.

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:41.320
Just give me your hand already.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:47.110
I guess this is pretty surprising, right?

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:48.780
These hands...

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:54.210
The hands of a candymaker, who tends to
mold candy melted at high temperatures...

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:55.580
are usually scarred.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.670
B... Beautiful!

00:21:57.670 --> 00:22:00.090
What beautiful hands!

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:03.420
These are truly the hands of a devoted artisan!

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:07.130
I’ve never seen a woman with such beautiful hands!

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:08.090
Huh?

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.180
You’re kidding, right?

00:22:10.180 --> 00:22:15.520
You’re the first person to have
thought of my hands in that manner.

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:17.990
Samurai Boy...

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:21.610
I get the feeling that something may be starting here.

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:22.980
And I get the feeling...

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:25.490
that this is where visiting hours end.

00:22:25.490 --> 00:22:26.320
Time’s up.

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:26.990
Let’s go.

00:24:04.980 --> 00:24:05.990
No way!

00:24:05.990 --> 00:24:08.280
If I lose, then the Japanese team will lose!

00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:10.270
I really just want to run away.

00:24:10.270 --> 00:24:11.350
You dumb chicken!

00:24:11.350 --> 00:24:12.490
M-Manager?!

00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:15.100
We’ve arrived in Monaco, dumbass!

00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:16.460
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.460 --> 00:24:17.210
Victory!!

00:24:17.210 --> 00:24:18.830
Revolutionizing the bread industry!

00:24:18.840 --> 00:24:19.900
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:22.650
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.120 --> 00:24:24.630
Hamburger buns.

00:24:24.630 --> 00:24:26.550
The perfect ratio of their thickness is 4:6.

00:24:26.550 --> 00:24:29.010
The lower jaw of a human is stronger than the upper jaw.

00:24:29.010 --> 00:24:31.670
So, if you make a sandwich
at this ratio, it’s easy to eat.

00:24:32.220 --> 00:24:34.140
Oh?!
